
=== an idle client reads nothing until the store says to
the first wait is entered before any cursor read: ok
and it offers nothing, never having read one: ok

=== a wake on a moved cursor reads it and applies what it points past
  cursor reads: 1, journal listings: 1
the cursor was read once: ok
and the journal listed once: ok
the token now offered is what that pass finished with: ok

=== a wake on an unmoved cursor costs the read and nothing more
  cursor reads: 1, journal listings: 0
the cursor was read again: ok
but the journal was not listed: ok
and the token is unchanged: ok

=== a pass that dies keeps offering the token it last finished with
  offered after the failed pass: 0000000000100-peer
the moved cursor is not offered: ok
the token is the one from the last clean pass: ok

=== and it advances again once a pass completes
the token has caught up with the cursor: ok
a token off a body compares equal to one off the wire: ok
